{"content_hash": "1b7920ccfb92df9e", "version_id": 682, "article_id": 69, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Dad fined €3,000 after son, 2, dies in Cyprus hotel fall", "title_zh": "两岁儿子在塞浦路斯酒店坠亡，父亲被罚3000欧元", "has_translation": true, "topic": "world", "source": "bbc_world", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvj6j1klez88o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1437943085269-6da5dd4295bf?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MTB8fGRhZCUyMGZpbmVkJTIwc29ufGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTIxOTQ0ODR8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Steven Van Loy on Unsplash", "author": "Steven Van Loy", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@mafalou?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/man-wears-blue-crew-neck-t-shirt-holding-toddler-wears-black-hooded-jacket-near-ocean-under-blue-sky-at-daytime-oUhSla4L_98?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(165, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(203, 46%, 48%)", "label": "WORLD", "seed": "f11dca163925"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-17", "word_count": 135, "reading_minutes": 0.7, "lead": "A father from Essex lost his two-year-old son in a hotel fall in Cyprus. A court fined him €3,000 for causing the death.", "lead_zh": "一位来自埃塞克斯的父亲在塞浦路斯一家酒店失去了两岁的儿子。法院判他缴纳3000欧元罚款，理由是造成儿子死亡。", "preview": "Joshua Foster, 37, was on holiday with his family in Cyprus. On 12 July, he put his son on a windowsill at a five-star hotel. He thought the", "preview_zh": "37岁的约书亚·福斯特正在塞浦路斯与家人度假。7月12日，他把儿子放在一家五星级酒店的窗台上。他以为窗户是关着的。男孩从近40英尺高处坠落。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 672, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/69/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 43.925, "size_bytes": 264528, "engine": "kokoro", "voice": "af_heart", "word_count": 154, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@2e11152/content/data/versions/682.json", "paragraphs": ["Joshua Foster, 37, was on holiday with his family in Cyprus. On 12 July, he put his son on a windowsill at a five-star hotel. He thought the window was closed. The boy fell almost 40 feet.", "The child was taken to hospital but died. Foster told a court he lost control of his son. He admitted causing death through a reckless act. A judge fined him €3,000.", "The judge said Foster did not mean to put his son in danger. She called it a momentary error. Foster spent eight days in custody. He said he wants to go home to his wife and daughter.", "The family said their son was deeply loved and will be forever missed. Foster's lawyer said the case should never have gone to court. He called Foster an incredible father."], "paragraphs_zh": ["37岁的约书亚·福斯特正在塞浦路斯与家人度假。7月12日，他把儿子放在一家五星级酒店的窗台上。他以为窗户是关着的。男孩从近40英尺高处坠落。", "孩子被送往医院，但不幸去世。福斯特在法庭上说，他没能抓住儿子。他承认因鲁莽行为导致儿子死亡。法官判他罚款3000欧元。", "法官说，福斯特并非有意让儿子处于危险之中。她称这是一时失误。福斯特被拘留了八天。他说想回家和妻子、女儿团聚。", "家人说，儿子深受疼爱，将永远被怀念。福斯特的律师说，此案本不该上法庭。他称福斯特是一位了不起的父亲。"], "body": "Joshua Foster, 37, was on holiday with his family in Cyprus. On 12 July, he put his son on a windowsill at a five-star hotel. He thought the window was closed. The boy fell almost 40 feet.\n\nThe child was taken to hospital but died. Foster told a court he lost control of his son. He admitted causing death through a reckless act. A judge fined him €3,000.\n\nThe judge said Foster did not mean to put his son in danger. She called it a momentary error. Foster spent eight days in custody. He said he wants to go home to his wife and daughter.\n\nThe family said their son was deeply loved and will be forever missed. Foster's lawyer said the case should never have gone to court. He called Foster an incredible father.", "body_zh": "37岁的约书亚·福斯特正在塞浦路斯与家人度假。7月12日，他把儿子放在一家五星级酒店的窗台上。他以为窗户是关着的。男孩从近40英尺高处坠落。\n\n孩子被送往医院，但不幸去世。福斯特在法庭上说，他没能抓住儿子。他承认因鲁莽行为导致儿子死亡。法官判他罚款3000欧元。\n\n法官说，福斯特并非有意让儿子处于危险之中。她称这是一时失误。福斯特被拘留了八天。他说想回家和妻子、女儿团聚。\n\n家人说，儿子深受疼爱，将永远被怀念。福斯特的律师说，此案本不该上法庭。他称福斯特是一位了不起的父亲。", "text": "Joshua Foster, 37, was on holiday with his family in Cyprus. On 12 July, he put his son on a windowsill at a five-star hotel. He thought the window was closed. The boy fell almost 40 feet. The child was taken to hospital but died. Foster told a court he lost control of his son. He admitted causing death through a reckless act. A judge fined him €3,000. The judge said Foster did not mean to put his son in danger. She called it a momentary error. Foster spent eight days in custody. He said he wants to go home to his wife and daughter. The family said their son was deeply loved and will be forever missed. Foster's lawyer said the case should never have gone to court. He called Foster an incredible father.", "vocab": [{"word": "fine", "pos": "verb", "zh": "罚款", "note": "常用被动语态：be fined + 金额", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "fall", "pos": "verb", "zh": "坠落；跌倒", "note": "过去式 fell，过去分词 fallen", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "window", "pos": "noun", "zh": "窗户", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "hotel", "pos": "noun", "zh": "酒店", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "hospital", "pos": "noun", "zh": "医院", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "court", "pos": "noun", "zh": "法庭", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "judge", "pos": "noun", "zh": "法官", "note": "也可作动词，意为“判断”", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "lawyer", "pos": "noun", "zh": "律师", "note": "", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Dad fined after son, 2, died in Cyprus hotel fall", "summary_original": "Joshua Foster \"lost control\" of his son while showing him the view of a water park from a window.", "body_original": "Dad fined after son, 2, died in Cyprus hotel fall\nBy\nLewis Adams\nEssex\nPublished\n16 October 2026, 10:31 BST\nUpdated 9 hours ago\nA father whose two-year-old boy fell from a fourth floor window of a Cyprus hotel has been fined €3,000 (£2,500) for causing his death.\nJoshua Foster thought the window was closed when he placed his son on a sill to show him the view of a waterpark\nand \"lost control\" of him\n, Paphos District Court previously heard.\nThe toddler fell nearly 40ft (12.1m) at the five-star King Evelthon Beach Hotel and Resort on 12 July, the first day of the family's holiday in Chlorakas.\nFoster, 37, from Essex, admitted causing death through a reckless, rash or dangerous act and was sentenced earlier.\nHe told reporters afterwards: \"Thank you for the support. I'm looking forward to going home and being with my wife and daughter.\"\nLater, the family said in a statement: \"We are relieved that this process is now over, but for our family, the consequences of this tragedy will never end.\n\"Our son was deeply loved and will be forever missed. His loss is something we carry with us every day.\"\nFoster, an auditor, arrived in Cyprus hours before the incident with his wife, two children and in-laws.\nThey enjoyed various activities and swimming, before getting ready for dinner in the evening.\nAt about 18:00, Foster, his father-in-law and son were walking towards a lift when the boy noticed a waterpark outside.\nFoster pushed the lift button, placed the child on the windowsill and the \"inconceivable\" unfolded before he could react, the court heard.\nThe boy was taken to Paphos General Hospital and later pronounced dead.\n\"The window did not appear to carry markings that would necessarily have alerted the defendant to the fact that one section was open,\" said District Judge Froso Christodoulidou.\nHis failure to establish that the window was not closed led to the tragic result, the judge added.\n\"It was a momentary error which created a dangerous situation with fatal consequences,\" he said.\nThe judge added there was \"no evidence that the defendant deliberately exposed the child to danger\", according to a translation of proceedings.\nShe added no sentence could outweigh the \"personal consequences of the loss of his child\".\nIn a voluntary statement to police, Foster said when he placed his son on the windowsill, the boy \"fell before he had a chance to grab him\".\nWhile Foster had alcohol in his system, it did not form a significant part of the case against him and his lawyer Alexandros Alexandrou said there was no testimony he was drunk.\nAfter the sentencing, Foster's lawyer, Alexandros Alexandrou, told reporters the case should have \"never gone to court\".\nHe said Foster was held in custody for eight days immediately after the incident and he had to call his daughter from custody to explain what had happened.\n\"Within this three months, there was a lost opportunity for this man to grieve as he wanted to, to be with his family,\" he said.\nHe described his client as an \"incredible father\".\n\"[He is] an exemplary family man with a beautiful family behind him, that support him, that embraces him, that has always been by his side.\"\nDo you have a story suggestion for Essex? Contact us below.\nGet in touch\nYour Voice\nContact form\nContact form\nFollow Essex news on\nBBC Sounds\n,\nFacebook\n,\nexternal\n,\nInstagram\n,\nexternal\nand\nX\n,\nexternal\n.\nRelated topics\nEssex\nPaphos\nCyprus\nMore on this story\nDad sees son fall to death from Cyprus hotel window\nPublished\n6 October\nFather admits causing death of his son in hotel fall\nPublished\n22 September\nRelated internet links\nHM Courts & Tribunals Service", "fetched_at": "2026-10-16T23:48:02.449828", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Joshua", "s": 0.325, "e": 0.725, "sm": 325, "em": 724, "cs": 0, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Foster", "s": 0.725, "e": 1.225, "sm": 725, "em": 1225, "cs": 7, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 1.225, "e": 1.3, "sm": 1225, "em": 1299, "cs": 13, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "37", "s": 1.3, "e": 2.0, "sm": 1300, "em": 2000, "cs": 15, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": ",", "s": 2.0, "e": 2.05, "sm": 2000, "em": 2049, 